        <p>
          Peristaltic pumping is a technology with a surprisingly long supply chain. The pump itself is simple — rollers squeeze a tube, the tube does the work — but the companies that build it range from century-old industrial fluid-handling houses to specialist OEM factories that quietly supply half the private-label pumps sold online. For a buyer in 2026, the hard part is rarely understanding the technology; it is knowing which supplier to trust for a specific job, budget and volume.
        </p>
        <p>
          This guide profiles ten manufacturers that appear most often in real purchasing conversations: who they are, what they are known for, where they are strong, and who typically buys from them. "Top" here means widely used and widely referenced across their segments — not a claim that any single company is right for every application. We close with a comparison table, a four-step selection process, and the questions buyers ask us most.
        </p>

        <h2 id="how-to-read">How to Read This List</h2>
        <p>
          The ten companies below split roughly into two groups. The first five are Western brands with decades of history, global service networks and premium pricing — they suit regulated industries, high-value fluids and buyers who need local support. The second five are Chinese manufacturers, mostly built around the Baoding, Hebei pump cluster, that compete on value, OEM/ODM flexibility and export experience — they suit distributors, integrators and volume buyers. Both groups are capable; the right choice depends on your application, not on a brand name.
        </p>

        <h2 id="watson-marlow">1. Watson-Marlow (UK)</h2>
        <p>
          Watson-Marlow is the name most engineers associate with the modern peristaltic pump. Based in Falmouth, UK, and part of the Spirax-Sarco group, the company developed tube-squeezing pump technology in the 1950s and has built a reputation across biopharma, food, beverage and chemical dosing. Its range spans laboratory drives, industrial process pumps, chemical metering units and bioprocess transfer and filling systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> deep engineering resources, rigorous documentation for regulated environments, and a worldwide service footprint. <strong>Best for:</strong> buyers in pharma, food and specialty chemical processing who need validated performance, local support and are willing to pay a premium.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cole-parmer">2. Cole-Parmer / Masterflex (US)</h2>
        <p>
          Cole-Parmer is a long-established US laboratory supply house, and Masterflex is its peristaltic pump brand — one of the most recognized names in lab pumping. Masterflex drives and heads, together with a huge tubing catalog, are staples in universities, R&amp;D labs and pilot plants. The ecosystem is a strength: sizing a pump, choosing a tube and ordering spares is unusually easy because everything is listed in one catalog.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> convenience, breadth of tubing options, fast delivery and dependable sizing tools. <strong>Best for:</strong> laboratories, research groups and maintenance teams that value quick sourcing and standardized parts over the lowest price.
        </p>

        <h2 id="graco">3. Graco (US)</h2>
        <p>
          Graco, headquartered in Minneapolis, is one of the larger industrial fluid-handling companies in the world, known for pumps and equipment across painting, lubrication, sealant and adhesive applications. Its peristaltic offering is built for tough industrial duty — moving abrasive, viscous or aggressive fluids that would damage other pump types. The company's distribution network and service parts availability are strong points in industrial markets.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> rugged construction, industrial-grade durability and a mature global distribution channel. <strong>Best for:</strong> manufacturing plants and maintenance contractors handling abrasive or heavy fluids who want a supplier with local industrial support.
        </p>

        <h2 id="blue-white">4. Blue-White (US)</h2>
        <p>
          Blue-White, based in California, has specialized in chemical metering for decades and is well known for its Flex-Pro line of peristaltic metering pumps and chemical feed systems. The company's pumps are common in water and wastewater treatment, pool and spa chemical dosing, and agricultural injection. Their pump heads are designed for quick tube changes in the field, which matters to operators who service pumps regularly.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> deep water-treatment domain experience, serviceable heads and solid panel-mount and wall-mount options. <strong>Best for:</strong> water treatment contractors, pool chemical suppliers and facilities that dose chlorine or other treatment chemicals.
        </p>

        <h2 id="stenner">5. Stenner (US)</h2>
        <p>
          Stenner, a Florida-based manufacturer, has built a classic franchise on simple, reliable fixed-speed peristaltic dosing pumps. The brand is a common sight on residential well systems, commercial water treatment installations and pool chemical feeders, where its straightforward design and easy-to-replace parts have earned a loyal following among installers.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> simplicity, field serviceability and widely stocked replacement parts. <strong>Best for:</strong> well-water treatment, pool and spa dosing and small commercial water systems where operators want a pump their local technician can service without special tools.
        </p>

        <h2 id="lead-fluid-longer">6. Lead Fluid &amp; Longer (China, Baoding)</h2>
        <p>
          Baoding, in China's Hebei province, is the historic heart of the country's peristaltic pump industry, and Lead Fluid (Lead Fluid Technology) and Longer are its two best-known brands. Both companies supply laboratory peristaltic pumps, industrial dosing pumps and OEM pump heads, and both have exported for years through distributors and integrators worldwide. For many overseas buyers, these are the first names they meet when sourcing value-priced peristaltic hardware.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> competitive pricing, broad model ranges and genuine OEM/ODM capability built over years of export work. <strong>Best for:</strong> distributors, lab suppliers and equipment integrators who need cost-effective pumps with customization options.
        </p>

        <h2 id="chonry">7. Chonry / CR Pump (China)</h2>
        <p>
          Chonry, often trading as CR Pump, is a Chinese manufacturer with a strong orientation toward peristaltic pump heads and drive customization. Rather than chasing a broad catalog, the company is frequently found behind OEM and private-label projects, supplying heads and drives to equipment makers who build pumps into instruments, analyzers and dispensing machines.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> flexible customization, modular head-and-drive combinations and responsive engineering communication. <strong>Best for:</strong> instrument and machinery manufacturers integrating a pump into their own product, and private-label buyers who need the pump built to their spec.
        </p>

        <h2 id="prefluid">8. Prefluid (China)</h2>
        <p>
          Prefluid is a Chinese peristaltic pump manufacturer with a practical range covering laboratory transfer, industrial dosing and chemical feed applications. The brand is most often encountered through importers and distributors who value a balance between standard catalog breadth and value pricing, and it is a reasonable option for water treatment and light industrial projects with straightforward requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> value pricing, a standard range that covers common duties, and export-oriented service. <strong>Best for:</strong> importers, distributors and end users in water treatment or light industry who want dependable basic performance without premium pricing.
        </p>

        <h2 id="jihpump">9. JIHPUMP (China)</h2>
        <p>
          JIHPUMP is a Chinese peristaltic pump manufacturer serving both laboratory and light industrial buyers with pumps, pump heads and tubing. The company is a typical example of the export-ready Baoding-style supplier: catalog-driven, quick to quote, and comfortable with OEM work. Its pumps appear in lab supply catalogs and e-commerce channels aimed at research and small-scale production.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> broad catalog coverage, fast quoting and flexible OEM service. <strong>Best for:</strong> lab distributors, online sellers and OEM integrators who need a responsive, cost-effective source for standard pump configurations.
        </p>

        <h2 id="kamoer">10. Kamoer (China, Shanghai)</h2>
        <p>
          Kamoer, based in Shanghai, has built one of the more visible Chinese peristaltic pump brands among global lab users and makers. Its compact lab pumps and dosing pumps are widely sold through online channels, which makes the brand especially familiar to researchers, students and small-scale equipment builders. Kamoer's accessible pricing and active product community give it unusually strong brand recognition for a Chinese pump manufacturer.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Strengths:</strong> approachable pricing, compact design and strong online availability. <strong>Best for:</strong> laboratories, schools, hobbyist and maker projects, and light dosing applications where ease of purchase matters more than industrial certification.
        </p>

